{"items":[{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-3tgsighve4rdan1of6vcte-1","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-3tgsighve4rdan1of6vcte-1","dateCreated":"2026-08-18T22:51:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-08-18T23:46:36+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) now enables AWS workloads in the AWS European Sovereign Cloud (Germany) Region to securely authenticate with external services using short-lived JSON Web Tokens (JWTs). The AWS European Sovereign Cloud is an independent cloud for Europe entirely located within the European Union (EU), designed to help customers meet their evolving sovereignty requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nWith outbound identity federation, AWS workloads can securely authenticate with third-party cloud providers, SaaS providers, and self-hosted applications without using long-term credentials or implementing complex workarounds. Customers can exchange their AWS IAM credentials for cryptographically signed, short-lived JWTs, providing a simple and secure mechanism to access external services. These tokens contain rich context about the AWS workloads, enabling external services to implement fine-grained access control. Administrators can control access to token generation and enforce token properties (such as lifetime, audience, and signing algorithms) using IAM policies and audit token usage using CloudTrail logs, allowing them to meet their organization\u0027s security and compliance requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/identity/federation/outbound-federation/\"\u003eoutbound identity federation product page\u003c/a\u003e, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_outbound.html\"\u003eIAM user guide\u003c/a\u003e, or read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/simplify-access-to-external-services-using-aws-iam-outbound-identity-federation/\"\u003eAWS News Blog Post\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/08/aws-iam-european-sovereign-cloud/","postDateTime":"2026-08-18T22:30:00Z","headline":"AWS IAM identity federation to external services is now available in AWS European Sovereign Cloud Region"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-iam","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-iam","description":"general:products/aws-iam","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:26+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-security-token-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-security-token-service","description":"general:products/aws-security-token-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:17:15+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-identity-and-access-management","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-identity-and-access-management","description":"general:products/aws-identity-and-access-management","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:03:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:03:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#security-identity-and-compliance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"security-identity-and-compliance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/security-identity-and-compliance","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-hyywnfhmzgeudjjp8jsii8","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-hyywnfhmzgeudjjp8jsii8","dateCreated":"2025-11-20T20:04:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-01T23:16:00+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Security Token Service (STS) now supports Internet Protocol version 6 (IPv6) addresses via new dual-stack endpoints. You can connect to STS over the public internet using IPv6, IPv4, or dual-stack (both IPv4 and IPv6) clients. Dual-stack support is also available when you access STS endpoints privately from your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) using AWS PrivateLink, allowing you to invoke STS APIs without traversing the public internet.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nSupport for dual-stack STS endpoints is available in all AWS Commercial Regions, AWS GovCloud (US) Regions, and China Regions. To get started, configure your STS client to use the new dual-stack endpoints using the configuration instructions in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_dual-stack_endpoint_support.html\"\u003eIAM user guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/11/aws-sts-ipv6/","postDateTime":"2025-11-21T08:00:00Z","headline":"AWS Security Token Service Now Supports Internet Protocol version 6 (IPv6)"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-identity-and-access-management","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-identity-and-access-management","description":"general:products/aws-identity-and-access-management","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:03:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:03:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#security-identity-and-compliance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"security-identity-and-compliance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/security-identity-and-compliance","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-security-token-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-security-token-service","description":"general:products/aws-security-token-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:17:15+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1742471204","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-8tv84e1Fy9KCJSGVXGSdZy","dateCreated":"2025-04-17T16:42:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-04-18T19:00:02+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) now automatically serves all requests to the global endpoint (sts.amazonaws.com) in the same AWS Region as your deployed workloads, enhancing resiliency and performance. Previously, all requests to the STS global endpoint were served from the US East (N. Virginia) Region.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nWith this enhancement, your applications benefit from improved latency and fault isolation as requests are processed in the same Region as your workloads. For example, if your application runs in US West (Oregon) and calls the STS global endpoint, your requests are now served locally in US West (Oregon) instead of being routed to US East (N. Virginia).\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThis update is available in all AWS Regions that are enabled by default. No action is required from customers to benefit from these improvements. Any requests to the STS global endpoint from Regions not enabled by default (i.e. opt-in Regions) will continue to be served in US East (N. Virginia).\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nWe continue to recommend that you use the appropriate \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdkref/latest/guide/feature-sts-regionalized-endpoints.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSTS Regional endpoints\u003c/a\u003e whenever possible. For more information about these changes, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_temp_region-endpoints.html#reference_sts_global_endpoint_changes\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS STS global endpoint changes\u003c/a\u003e , and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/security/announcing-upcoming-changes-to-the-aws-security-token-service-global-endpoint/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eannouncement blogpost.\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/04/aws-sts-global-endpoint-requests-locally-regions-default/","postDateTime":"2025-04-18T10:00:00-07:00","headline":"AWS STS global endpoint now serves your requests locally in regions enabled by default"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#security-identity-and-compliance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"security-identity-and-compliance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/security-identity-and-compliance","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-security-token-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-security-token-service","description":"general:products/aws-security-token-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:17:15+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-06-aws-security-token-supports-privatelink-in-us-eu-asia-pacific","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/aws-security-token-supports-privatelink-in-us-eu-asia-pacific/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:30:06+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/Welcome.html\"\u003eAWS Security Token Service\u003c/a\u003e supports \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e in US East (Virginia), US East (Ohio), EU (Ireland), and Asia Pacific (Tokyo) regions, enabling you to route data between your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and Security Token Service entirely within the AWS network.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Security Token Service is a web service that enables you to request temporary, limited-privilege credentials you can use to access your AWS resources. By using Security Token Service with Amazon VPC endpoints, you can now keep credential-related, encrypted communication within the AWS network and help meet your compliance and regulatory requirements to limit public internet connectivity. You can also use VPC endpoint policies to control access to Security Token Service resources in your network.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupport for AWS PrivateLink in AWS Security Token Service is available in the following regions:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e• US East (N. Virginia)\u003cbr\u003e\n• US East (Ohio)\u003cbr\u003e\n• US West (Oregon)\u003cbr\u003e\n• EU (Ireland)\u003cbr\u003e\n• Asia Pacific (Tokyo)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGet started by reading the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/Welcome.html\"\u003eAWS Security Token Service User Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:25Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/aws-security-token-supports-privatelink-in-us-eu-asia-pacific/","postDateTime":"2019-06-26T14:31:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Security Token Service Now Supports AWS PrivateLink in US East (Virginia), US East (Ohio), EU (Ireland), Asia Pacific (Tokyo)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/Welcome.html\"\u003eAWS Security Token Service\u003c/a\u003e supports \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/privatelink.html\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e in US East (Virginia), US East (Ohio), EU (Ireland), and Asia Pacific (Tokyo) regions, enabling you to route data between your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and Security Token Service entirely within the AWS network.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#security-identity-and-compliance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"security-identity-and-compliance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/security-identity-and-compliance","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-vpc","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-vpc","description":"general:products/amazon-vpc","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-identity-and-access-management","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-identity-and-access-management","description":"general:products/aws-identity-and-access-management","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:03:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:03:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-benefits-realized#security","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-benefits-realized","name":"security","description":"marketing:benefits-realized/security","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:28+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-security-token-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-security-token-service","description":"general:products/aws-security-token-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:17:15+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-iam","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-iam","description":"general:products/aws-iam","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:26+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-07-aws-sts-support-for-privatelink-us-west-2","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/aws-sts-support-for-privatelink-us-west-2/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:26:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:56:50+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/Welcome.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Security Token Service\u003c/a\u003e supports \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e in the US West (Oregon) region, enabling you to route data between your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and Security Token Service entirely within the AWS network.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Security Token Service is a web service that enables you to request temporary, limited-privilege credentials for AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) users or for users that you authenticate (federated users). By using Security Token Service with Amazon VPC endpoints, you can now keep credential-related, encrypted communication within the AWS network and help meet your compliance and regulatory requirements to limit public internet connectivity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupport for AWS PrivateLink in AWS Security Token Service is available in the US West (Oregon) region. Learn more by reading the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/Welcome.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Security Token Service User Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:21Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/aws-sts-support-for-privatelink-us-west-2/","postDateTime":"2018-07-31T13:09:42Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Security Token Service Now Supports AWS PrivateLink in US West (Oregon) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/Welcome.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Security Token Service\u003c/a\u003e supports \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e in the US West (Oregon) region, enabling you to route data between your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and Security Token Service entirely within the AWS network.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-security-token-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-security-token-service","description":"general:products/aws-security-token-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:17:15+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-vpc","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-vpc","description":"general:products/amazon-vpc","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"}]}],"metadata":{"count":5,"totalHits":5},"fieldTypes":{"regionalAvailability":"LongText","nofollow":"Boolean","date":"Date","language":"Text","title":"Text","postDateTime":"DateTime","body":"Text","postSummary":"LongText","ctaLabel":"Text","mediaThumbnail":"Text","nosnippet":"Boolean","price":"Text","ctaLink":"URL","headline":"Text","contentType":"Text","bodyBack":"LongText","secondaryCTALabel":"Text","primaryCTALink":"URL","noindex":"Boolean","level":"Text","heading":"Text","mediaType":"Text","mediaAlt":"Text","headlineUrl":"Text","mediaSrc":"URL","durationMinutes":"Number","badge":"JSON","videoImageUrl":"URL","postBody":"LongText","secondaryCTALink":"URL","Video":"URL","modifiedDate":"DateTime","namePerson":"Text","location":"Text","time":"Text","publishedDate":"DateTime","durationReadtime":"Number","primaryCTALabel":"Text"}}